### Template for manual API testing with the VS Code REST Client extension.
###
### Copy this to a working file before filling anything in:
###   cp requests.http.example requests.http
###
### Every *.http file is gitignored (see .gitignore) precisely so the token
### you paste below never reaches git. This .example file is the exception —
### it IS tracked, so never paste a real token or password into it.

@host = http://localhost:3001


### ============================================================
### AUTH
### ============================================================

### Register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "REPLACE_ME"
}

### Login — run this, then copy `token` from the response body
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "REPLACE_ME"
}

###

### Paste the token from the login response above.
### Tokens expire after 1h, so expect to redo this between sessions.
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### AUTHENTICATED REQUESTS
### ============================================================

### No X-CSRF-Token header is needed on writes here. `authenticate`
### (src/middleware.js) accepts an Authorization: Bearer header when no auth
### cookie is present, and `verifyCsrf` returns early in that same
### no-cookie case. A browser, which does send the cookie, gets the full
### double-submit check instead.

### List injuries
GET {{host}}/api/injuries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an injury
POST {{host}}/api/injuries
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Lower back pain",
  "bodyArea": "Lower back",
  "side": "Left",
  "startDate": "2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "cause": "Deadlift",
  "description": "Started after heavy lifting at the gym",
  "status": "Active"
}

###

### Set this from the id the create returned, then use it in nested routes.
@injuryId = 1

### Add a symptom to that injury
POST {{host}}/api/injuries/{{injuryId}}/symptoms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "date": "2025-01-02T00:00:00.000Z",
  "painLevel": 4,
  "location": "Lower back",
  "trigger": "Sitting too long",
  "duration": "2 hours",
  "notes": "Worse in the morning"
}
